            <ArticleTitle>Triptans: actions and reactions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>611-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2008.01077.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subcutaneous sumatriptan is superior to placebo in achieving headache relief. Some commonly reported adverse events are paresthesias, tingling, and transient worsening of headache. Why do patients develop these symptoms? Our unique case may shed light on its actions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
